  "review": {
    "review": "The hero was alive when the planner stopped. The initiating blockage was an unfinished piranha chest: D2996-D2997 showed hunger, unidentified potions, no known invisibility, no identify scroll or intuition stone, and no usable ordinary food. Known waterskin healing restored full health but did not supply an admitted preparation transaction. Pool preparation rejected hungry testing, while descent rejected the unfinished chest. Recovery then made four genuine moves before combat interrupted it. D3001-D3008 comprised combat item selections and targeting, yet every input consumed the navigation-stall allowance. D3009 stopped at eight such inputs despite full health. Accepted transitions distinguish advancing combat time from stationary targeting. The proposed correction charges navigation stalls only to inputs owned by that recovery incident; all inputs still consume the unchanged total recovery budget. It does not repair the original pool prerequisite problem or establish successful combat, descent or collection. The new reduced bookkeeping regression failed on the original policy and passed after correction. No runtime-memory reconstruction or changed-decision gameplay replay was performed.",
    "learnings": "Keep survival interruptions distinct from failed navigation attempts without granting unlimited recovery. Pool preparation still needs an executable, hunger-funded identification and protected retrieval plan; full health and unidentified potions alone do not establish one."
  },
